    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "The student must link identity and contradiction to gradient and intercept matching, using lines with an unknown parameter. Parts a to c are matching conditions with scaffolding. The hardest demand is parts d and e. Part d means expanding k(x+1)+2 and matching two coefficients for two unknowns. Part e needs the reframing that equal gradients with c ≠ 5 gives parallel lines, so a contradiction. This goes beyond classifying given equations (p55-q1, 32) but involves no heavy multi-step algebra or hidden insight.",
